Checkpoint for a session handoff (PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS §18.4.8.10). This commit is a recoverable state, not a finished change: the new regression and
integration tests are NOT written, 16 existing tests FAIL (4 in tests/core/cognitive/test_creative_content_anchor.py that pin the old response text, 9 in
tests/test_live_check_draft_plan.py and 3 in tests/test_live_check_repeat.py because the harness and the repeat tool call the changed builder API / cap -- see
handoff.md), and the full suite has not been run on it. Base: main f13bfdefcdd197ed1f966de0b1f93037a4168af4. DEBT-043's status is intentionally untouched.

core/cognitive/content_anchor.py
- render_clarification_response() / ClarificationRendering: a detector-specific question is returned ONLY together with (1) a truthful intent statement
  derived from the detector's own data (artifact kind + "no subject/premise") -- the raw request is no longer echoed as an "interpretation" -- and
  (2) at most 3 genuine planner steps, on separate numbered lines, in plan order, labelled "Provisional draft plan (not checked or approved; ...)", with
  omitted steps stated as omitted. Otherwise the generic SAFE_FAILURE_MESSAGE (proposed wording of the owner's directive §5.4, a proposed replacement for an
  unrecovered original) is returned and `failure_reason` is set.
- genuine_plan_steps(): skips non-string/empty/whitespace steps, strips list markers, and returns [] for the planner's degrade fallback (planner._decompose
  answers a failed/unparsable model call with ONE step equal to the goal description or "unspecified").
- build_clarification_question(): artifact-specific wording (story, poem, essay, song, joke + generic), no story-specific examples, no "is enough" promise
  (the detector needs >= 2 content tokens), keeps the real "surprise me" way-out (backed by _DELEGATION) and the stateless "send it again" instruction.
- build_clarification_response() kept as a thin string wrapper; its `interpretation` kwarg is replaced by `request_text` (used only to recognise the fallback).
core/orchestrator.py (CRLF preserved)
- the ESCALATE-surfacing block renders first: paired -> existing event orchestrator.clarification_requested (+ additive plan_steps_shown/plan_steps_total) and
  the paired text; not paired -> existing event orchestrator.query_failed (error_type ClarificationPairingUnavailable, reason code only, no internals) and the
  safe-failure text. No new governance evaluation, gate, model call or outcome type; the plan/governance sequence before this block is unchanged.
